WEBVTT

00:05.716 --> 00:08.549
&lt;i>Larry was just a single dad&lt;/i>

00:08.719 --> 00:12.450
&lt;i>Till a toxic spill in the science lab&lt;/i>

00:12.623 --> 00:17.322
&lt;i>Gave him super strength
And x-ray eyes&lt;/i>

00:17.494 --> 00:22.329
&lt;i>He cooks, he cleans and now he flies&lt;/i>

00:22.499 --> 00:23.932
&lt;i>Superdad&lt;/i>

00:25.469 --> 00:27.835
&lt;i>He's a Superdad&lt;/i>

00:29.373 --> 00:34.037
&lt;i>He's a whiz in the kitchen
Makes potatoes au gratin&lt;/i>

00:37.481 --> 00:42.180
&lt;i>While helping the government
Find Osama Bin Laden&lt;/i>

00:45.756 --> 00:47.519
- Oh, hey.
- What's that?

00:47.691 --> 00:50.387
I'm writing a theme song
for a new sitcom on Nickelodeon.

00:50.561 --> 00:53.826
Does the show suck
as much as the song?

00:57.000 --> 01:00.197
- Who the hell are you?
- My friend Eldridge. He plays drums.

01:00.370 --> 01:02.998
Okay. That explains the bad attitude.

01:03.173 --> 01:06.734
- What, you're ragging on my name?
- No, I'm ragging on your instrument.

01:07.544 --> 01:09.034
Now beat it, I'm busy.

01:09.880 --> 01:13.043
- He said "beat it."
- And "instrument."

01:17.521 --> 01:20.752
&lt;i>Fighting crime and packing lunches&lt;/i>

01:20.924 --> 01:24.416
&lt;i>Changing diapers
And throwing punches&lt;/i>

01:26.496 --> 01:30.057
Little turd was right. This does suck.

01:31.101 --> 01:33.126
- Hey.
- Hey.

01:33.303 --> 01:35.601
- Jake's friend show up?
- Yeah, he's here.

01:35.772 --> 01:39.037
- When's he leaving?
- I said he could spend the night.

01:39.209 --> 01:41.404
Really?
Did you consider clearing it with me?

01:41.578 --> 01:43.773
You would've said no
to Jake having a friend over?

01:43.947 --> 01:47.576
If you recall, seven years ago
I said no to having Jake over.

01:47.751 --> 01:51.050
And yet, here he is.
So, what's the point in asking?

01:51.888 --> 01:55.289
Fine. What do we know
about the little drummer boy?

01:55.459 --> 01:58.428
Not much. Jake says
he's one of the cool kids at school.

01:58.595 --> 02:00.426
Then why's he hanging out with Jake?

02:00.964 --> 02:02.591
Are you saying my son's not cool?

02:02.766 --> 02:05.735
Your son got his tongue stuck
to the freezer last weekend.

02:05.902 --> 02:07.563
That could have happened to anybody.

02:07.738 --> 02:11.401
Anybody who tried to pick up
an Eskimo Pie with their tongue.

02:11.808 --> 02:15.266
- His hands were full.
- With a honey-baked ham.

02:15.979 --> 02:18.607
Okay, so he's not cool,
and he eats a lot of crap...

02:18.782 --> 02:23.310
...and his grades aren't the best, and
his personal hygiene is a little sketchy.

02:24.054 --> 02:25.954
Is there a "but" coming?

02:26.456 --> 02:29.186
But he's my son...

02:29.359 --> 02:32.089
...and I love him.

02:34.431 --> 02:35.659
What's so funny?

02:35.832 --> 02:38.323
Mom says the same thing about you.

02:39.169 --> 02:41.160
Really? Mom says she loves me?

03:14.171 --> 03:17.368
&lt;i>He's a member of the PTA&lt;/i>

03:17.541 --> 03:21.500
&lt;i>He wears leotards
But he's not gay&lt;/i>

03:21.678 --> 03:23.077
&lt;i>Superdad&lt;/i>

03:24.781 --> 03:25.805
&lt;i>He's a Sup...&lt;/i>

03:29.219 --> 03:31.687
Stupid drummers.

03:41.932 --> 03:44.526
Hey, hey, hey.

03:44.701 --> 03:45.929
Hey.

03:47.571 --> 03:49.198
I'm trying to work out there.

03:49.806 --> 03:52.104
Well, what do you think
we're doing in here, man?

03:52.309 --> 03:54.504
Don't feed me straight lines, Alfalfa.

03:55.846 --> 03:57.404
Just keep it down.

04:01.017 --> 04:02.382
Alfalfa?

04:02.552 --> 04:06.545
He gives everyone nicknames.
I'm Pumpkinhead, my dad's the Sponge.

04:07.057 --> 04:09.116
Don't even ask
what he calls my grandma.

04:09.326 --> 04:11.624
It rhymes with "bitch."

04:12.229 --> 04:14.595
Oh, wait, it is bitch.

04:16.032 --> 04:18.057
It rhymes with, uh...

04:18.568 --> 04:20.559
- Ditch?
- No.

04:21.071 --> 04:23.266
- Snitch?
- No.

04:23.774 --> 04:26.572
- Itch?
- No.

04:27.778 --> 04:29.541
Man, this is boring.

04:29.713 --> 04:31.613
Hold on, I'll think of it.

04:31.782 --> 04:33.647
No,
I mean what are we gonna do tonight?

04:34.151 --> 04:37.143
- I don't know, what do you wanna do?
- I don't know.

04:37.354 --> 04:39.413
Well, I don't know either.

04:40.457 --> 04:42.948
Hey, why don't we steal some beer
from your fridge...

04:43.126 --> 04:45.594
...go down to the beach
and get wasted?

04:45.762 --> 04:49.425
Okay, but I gotta warn you,
I get kind of stupid when I drink.

04:49.933 --> 04:52.663
Don't worry,
you can leave the thinking to me.

04:54.504 --> 04:58.440
Hey, you know what?
It does rhyme with "ditch."

04:59.576 --> 05:01.407
What does?

05:05.148 --> 05:07.173
&lt;i>Daddy, is Mr. Boots dead?&lt;/i>

05:07.350 --> 05:09.818
&lt;i>J- Bob, you did
throw him out of a moving car.&lt;/i>

05:09.986 --> 05:12.955
&lt;i>That's never good for a house cat.&lt;/i>

05:13.123 --> 05:15.591
&lt;i>I thought they were
supposed to land on their feet.&lt;/i>

05:15.759 --> 05:19.525
&lt;i>And that's what he was trying
to do when he bounced off the FedEx truck.&lt;/i>

05:19.696 --> 05:22.494
&lt;i>But let me see what I can do.
Cover your eyes.&lt;/i>

05:22.666 --> 05:24.031
&lt;i>Okay.&lt;/i>

05:30.440 --> 05:32.806
&lt;i>Mr. Boots, you're okay!&lt;/i>

05:32.976 --> 05:36.673
&lt;i>Just remember,
he's only got five lives left.&lt;/i>

05:39.616 --> 05:42.141
Maybe my song doesn't suck enough.

05:42.319 --> 05:44.719
Hey. So where's Jake and Eldridge?

05:44.921 --> 05:48.049
Beats me. Last I saw, they were
stealing beer out of the fridge...

05:48.225 --> 05:49.692
...and sneaking out the back.

05:49.860 --> 05:51.657
They stole beer?

05:51.828 --> 05:54.160
They had to,
I locked up the hard stuff.

05:54.965 --> 05:55.989
Charlie.

05:56.166 --> 05:58.464
Relax,
how drunk can they get off a 12-pack?

05:59.803 --> 06:02.738
Damn it.
This had to be Eldridge's idea.

06:02.939 --> 06:05.533
- Jake would never think of it on his own.
- That's true.

06:05.709 --> 06:09.839
The last bright idea he had was to
pick up an Eskimo Pie with his tongue.

06:10.580 --> 06:12.241
I'd better go look for them.

06:12.449 --> 06:15.577
Good idea. Embarrass him
in front of his only guy friend.

06:15.752 --> 06:17.549
Eldridge isn't his only guy friend.

06:17.721 --> 06:19.211
Who else does he hang out with?

06:19.389 --> 06:22.984
And you can't count you, me,
or military recruiters.

06:23.493 --> 06:26.485
So, what, I'm supposed to do nothing?
They have to be punished.

06:26.663 --> 06:29.325
Don't worry,
the alcohol will punish them plenty.

06:29.499 --> 06:31.524
Yeah, that's really worked for you.

06:31.701 --> 06:34.898
Trust me, Alan. Inside, I'm suffering.

06:39.009 --> 06:41.102
Oh, the agony.

06:50.487 --> 06:53.786
- Beer's not so cool now, is it?
- Leave me alone.

06:55.625 --> 06:57.616
And you,
what is your mother gonna say?

07:00.997 --> 07:02.794
For God's sake, that's wicker.

07:03.300 --> 07:06.269
Hey. How we all doing in here?

07:11.608 --> 07:13.371
You should have stopped them.

07:13.543 --> 07:17.502
And miss out on this?
How's it hanging, Alfalfa?

07:19.582 --> 07:22.107
And you call yourself a drummer.

07:23.019 --> 07:26.216
Keith Moon is vomiting in his grave.

07:42.772 --> 07:44.467
That's really beautiful, Charlie.

07:45.108 --> 07:48.475
Thanks. I wrote it
before I got kicked out of Juilliard.

07:49.813 --> 07:52.805
I gotta ask. How did you go
from writing something like that...

07:52.983 --> 07:54.610
...to jingles and kid music?

07:55.251 --> 07:59.745
Well, after I left school, I came back
to L.A. Hoping to write film scores.

08:00.256 --> 08:03.987
But I met this advertising guy
who needed a song about toothpaste.

08:04.160 --> 08:08.961
Before I knew it, I was rhyming
"exhilaration" with "constipation."

08:09.132 --> 08:11.999
"Open doors" with "cold sores."

08:12.168 --> 08:14.659
And one I am particularly proud of:

08:14.838 --> 08:17.432
"Make a switch" with "feminine itch."

08:18.308 --> 08:22.540
I hear you. When I came out here,
I was hoping to be a dancer.

08:22.712 --> 08:24.145
Really?

08:24.681 --> 08:27.878
Yeah. Then I met pot and doughnuts.

08:28.084 --> 08:30.143
Before I knew it,
I was scrubbing toilets...

08:30.320 --> 08:32.811
...and hosing teenage barf
out of wicker baskets.

08:34.190 --> 08:36.522
Rhyme that, Beethoven.

08:40.263 --> 08:42.026
&lt;i>A- tisket, a-tasket&lt;/i>

08:42.198 --> 08:44.860
&lt;i>I'm barfing in a basket&lt;/i>

08:46.336 --> 08:48.998
That's what pays your salary, baby.

08:50.407 --> 08:53.103
Eldridge's mom.
I'm gonna give her a piece of my mind.

08:53.276 --> 08:54.743
Oh, just let it go.

08:54.911 --> 08:58.540
No, no, this is poor parenting on her part
and she needs to know about it.

08:58.715 --> 09:02.014
Hi. I'm here to pick up Eldridge.
I hope he wasn't too much trouble.

09:02.185 --> 09:05.313
Trouble? He was an angel. Come on in.

09:05.688 --> 09:06.712
Thanks.

09:08.091 --> 09:09.251
&lt;i>Superdad&lt;/i>

09:16.666 --> 09:17.826
Thank you so much, Alan.

09:18.001 --> 09:21.334
Eldridge is welcome anytime.
We single parents have to stick together.

09:21.504 --> 09:22.664
- Yeah.
- See you, buddy.

09:22.839 --> 09:24.204
Yeah, bite me.

09:24.374 --> 09:26.274
- I heard that, young man.
Good for you.

09:26.443 --> 09:27.842
- Get in the car.
- Can I drive?

09:28.011 --> 09:29.876
Not with a
suspended license you can't.

09:30.046 --> 09:32.947
You suck.
- And you're ruining my life!

09:33.383 --> 09:35.214
Okay, bye-bye.

09:42.592 --> 09:43.889
Yes?

09:44.060 --> 09:46.893
What happened to
giving her a piece of your mind?

09:47.263 --> 09:49.891
Oh, come on,
we both know what happened.

09:50.200 --> 09:54.261
Right. Piece of tail always trumps
piece of mind, doesn't it?

09:54.437 --> 09:56.564
What do you want?
She's a beautiful woman...

09:56.739 --> 10:00.470
...she's been through a tough divorce,
she's raising a teenage son by herself.

10:00.643 --> 10:03.771
Last thing she needs
is me dumping more problems in her lap.

10:03.947 --> 10:06.108
So what are your plans for her lap?

10:06.282 --> 10:09.649
- I don't know, I might call her. We'll see.
- You're unbelievable.

10:09.853 --> 10:13.254
Your son finally gets a friend
and you're gonna try to nail his mother?

10:13.423 --> 10:16.620
First of all, with a classy woman
like Lyndsey, there's no nailing.

10:16.793 --> 10:20.092
There's, uh, dating and bonding
and getting to know one another.

10:20.263 --> 10:22.629
Then, eventually,
consummating the relationship...

10:22.799 --> 10:24.596
...with mutual respect and caring.

10:24.767 --> 10:26.758
Oh, grow up.

10:27.403 --> 10:29.928
This is a hot divorced mom
from the Valley.

10:30.106 --> 10:33.007
You're gonna need three penises
and a set of jumper cables...

10:33.176 --> 10:34.768
...just to get her attention.

10:35.979 --> 10:37.412
You're disgusting.

10:37.580 --> 10:41.277
Hey, I'm not the one trying to bang
the drummer's mom slowly.

10:41.451 --> 10:42.679
Don't you judge me.

10:43.620 --> 10:45.247
Why not?

10:46.589 --> 10:49.023
You've slept with
one of Jake's teachers...

10:49.192 --> 10:54.186
...his den mother, his karate instructor,
his ballet teacher and his aunt.

10:54.697 --> 10:58.633
- Great, so five wrongs make a right.
- What?

10:58.801 --> 11:01.964
If I jump off a bridge and land on top
of some broad Jake knows...

11:02.138 --> 11:04.299
...that makes it okay
for you to do it too?

11:04.474 --> 11:05.498
What?

11:05.675 --> 11:08.041
I think I've made my point.

11:11.447 --> 11:13.005
What?

11:19.189 --> 11:21.157
I'm never gonna drink again.

11:22.425 --> 11:23.790
Quitter.

11:23.960 --> 11:27.293
- Charlie.
- Oh, right. Attaboy.

11:29.132 --> 11:31.066
Here's your wastebasket.

11:31.234 --> 11:35.568
I rinsed it out but there are still some
tiny chunks in the weave.

11:35.738 --> 11:38.434
Maybe you could use
your dad's Waterpik.

11:39.842 --> 11:43.869
- Give the kid a break, he's hung-over.
- Oh, the poor dear.

11:46.249 --> 11:49.707
Next time, tell your friends
to puke out the window.

11:52.355 --> 11:54.152
Wanna know
a sure-fire hangover cure?

11:55.725 --> 11:56.851
Never stop drinking.

11:58.561 --> 12:00.222
- Charlie.
- Let me finish.

12:00.396 --> 12:02.557
Or never start in the first place.

12:04.000 --> 12:07.163
See how I turned that around?
Bring it home, Dr. Cosby.

12:09.572 --> 12:13.406
All right. For starters, you and Eldridge
stole beer that did not belong to you.

12:13.576 --> 12:15.100
That is not how I raised you.

12:16.179 --> 12:19.740
Now to the issue of underage drinking.

12:20.083 --> 12:23.541
Not only is it against the law,
alcohol destroys brain cells.

12:23.720 --> 12:26.553
Alan. Alan, you gotta tailor the pitch
to the audience.

12:26.723 --> 12:28.554
- What do you mean?
- Forget brain cells.

12:29.058 --> 12:31.390
Jake, listen to me.
This is very important.

12:31.561 --> 12:34.086
Alcohol can make it tough
to get a boner.

12:35.231 --> 12:36.858
You're kidding.

12:38.768 --> 12:43.137
I can't tell you how many times I've said,
"This has never happened before."

12:44.507 --> 12:45.838
Huh.

12:48.044 --> 12:50.774
- Where you going?
- To check out your theory.

12:53.650 --> 12:57.108
Remember,
he's your son and you love him.

13:02.792 --> 13:05.317
Dr. Alan Harper. May I help you?

13:05.762 --> 13:07.286
Oh, hi, Lyndsey.

13:08.231 --> 13:09.755
No, no, you're not interrupting.

13:09.932 --> 13:12.765
Just doing some stomach crunches.
Hang on.

13:12.935 --> 13:14.425
And 1000.

13:14.604 --> 13:16.401
So, uh, what's up?

13:18.041 --> 13:21.033
Tonight? Sure, sure, I'd love to.

13:21.210 --> 13:23.440
Yeah, yeah, I know that place.

13:23.613 --> 13:26.810
Eight o'clock, perfect. See you then.

13:27.317 --> 13:29.842
How about that? She called me.
Wants to have drinks.

13:30.053 --> 13:33.250
- Nice. What are you gonna tell Jake?
- Who?

13:34.590 --> 13:36.581
I mean, uh, what do you mean?

13:36.759 --> 13:39.819
Are you gonna tell him you're
hooking up with his buddy's mom?

13:39.996 --> 13:43.329
First of all, nobody said anything
about hooking up, it's just drinks.

13:43.499 --> 13:47.833
And second of all, Jake went out and
had drinks last night and didn't tell me.

13:49.972 --> 13:52.532
Man, that's the most lame-ass
rationalization...

13:52.709 --> 13:55.303
...for questionable behavior
I've ever heard from you.

13:55.478 --> 13:56.570
Yeah, so?

13:57.213 --> 13:59.272
Kudos.

13:59.882 --> 14:02.783
Hey, Uncle Charlie, you were wrong.

14:12.161 --> 14:15.688
It is so nice to get out of the house
and spend time with another grownup.

14:15.865 --> 14:19.494
I know, heh. It's hard to be
a single parent. Thankless really.

14:19.669 --> 14:21.000
Tell me about it.

14:21.170 --> 14:22.865
- Dealing with the ex.
- Boundaries.

14:23.039 --> 14:24.597
- The loneliness.
- Frustration.

14:24.774 --> 14:26.833
- It's all worth it though.
- Oh, yeah.

14:27.009 --> 14:30.137
My son is the greatest gift of my life.

14:30.313 --> 14:34.010
Mine too. I can't imagine loving anything
more than I love Jake.

14:34.650 --> 14:37.483
- To our children.
- Our children.

14:38.921 --> 14:41.151
Tell me I'm a good mom!
You're a good mom.

14:41.324 --> 14:42.814
I'm a dirty mom.

14:42.992 --> 14:45.620
Oh, you're so dirty.

14:47.130 --> 14:50.258
Oh, uh, whoopsie. Automatic flusher.

14:50.633 --> 14:51.895
Do that again.

14:52.068 --> 14:53.365
Okay.

14:55.238 --> 14:58.298
Not the toilet!
Sorry! Sorry!

15:13.089 --> 15:15.387
Hey. Hey, hey, hey.

15:17.093 --> 15:18.856
Aren't you grounded?

15:19.028 --> 15:21.394
Um, no, I think that's just
when my dad's here.

15:22.532 --> 15:25.592
Get in the house. All of you.

15:26.602 --> 15:29.366
- I thought you were cool.
- No, you didn't.

15:32.241 --> 15:33.674
- How old are you?
- Sixteen.

15:33.843 --> 15:35.970
- What about you? That's what I thought.
- Same.

15:36.179 --> 15:38.704
- We were just going to the beach.
- Nobody asked you.

15:38.881 --> 15:41.406
Now, I want you to listen to this...

15:41.951 --> 15:45.478
...and tell me if it makes you wanna
watch the TV show.

15:46.189 --> 15:48.316
&lt;i>What?&lt;/i>

15:50.827 --> 15:53.955
&lt;i>Larry was just a single dad&lt;/i>

15:54.130 --> 15:57.395
&lt;i>Till a toxic spill in a science lab&lt;/i>

15:57.567 --> 16:01.059
&lt;i>Gave him super strength
And x-ray eyes&lt;/i>

16:01.237 --> 16:04.570
&lt;i>He cooks, he cleans and now he flies&lt;/i>

16:04.740 --> 16:05.968
&lt;i>Superdad&lt;/i>

16:07.610 --> 16:11.102
&lt;i>He's a super bad, fighting mad
College grad wearing plaid&lt;/i>

16:11.280 --> 16:12.474
&lt;i>Superdad&lt;/i>

16:16.152 --> 16:18.643
- Wow, that was great.
- Oh, my God, that was so good.

16:18.821 --> 16:20.982
- Absolutely fantastic.
- You wrote that?

16:21.491 --> 16:22.924
- You think?
Definitely.

16:23.092 --> 16:25.856
Oh, yeah.
Really makes you wanna see the show.

16:27.029 --> 16:29.327
Thanks. Thank you.

16:29.499 --> 16:32.764
All right, well,
I guess you guys all wanna get going.

16:32.935 --> 16:35.460
- Yeah, let's go.
Yeah.

16:36.506 --> 16:38.167
- Psst, Jake.
- Yeah?

16:38.341 --> 16:40.969
- Lf you got a choice, take the tall one.
- Why?

16:41.143 --> 16:43.509
Trust me. It's my superpower.

16:44.013 --> 16:45.037
Thanks.

16:47.517 --> 16:49.041
&lt;i>Super uncle&lt;/i>

16:58.995 --> 17:00.155
I'm back.

17:00.329 --> 17:03.321
Oh, good. I was starting to worry.

17:03.833 --> 17:05.630
How did it go with Jake?

17:05.968 --> 17:08.493
Hardly knew he was here.

17:09.805 --> 17:11.329
Can you keep a secret?

17:11.841 --> 17:15.333
The real question is:
"Can I remember a secret?"

17:15.511 --> 17:16.876
You were right.

17:17.046 --> 17:18.536
That's no secret.

17:18.714 --> 17:21.945
- No, I mean about Lyndsey.
- Who's Lyndsey?

17:22.485 --> 17:23.543
Eldridge's mom.

17:24.854 --> 17:26.344
Who's Eldridge?

17:26.923 --> 17:29.050
Jake's friend? The drummer?

17:29.225 --> 17:31.853
Anyway, we did wind up having sex.

17:32.528 --> 17:34.621
You and me?

17:35.865 --> 17:38.698
You really need to get into a program.

17:39.235 --> 17:41.169
It's not funny anymore.

17:41.337 --> 17:43.532
Humor is very subjective.

17:43.706 --> 17:46.300
Come on, be serious.
I'm telling you about Lyndsey...

17:46.475 --> 17:48.966
...because I may need you
to cover for me with Jake.

17:49.145 --> 17:51.705
- Don't worry, I got your back.
- Thanks, Charlie.

17:51.881 --> 17:54.008
- Good night.
- Good night.

17:59.388 --> 18:01.151
Is he gone?

18:01.324 --> 18:02.689
Who?

18:03.526 --> 18:06.222
- Dad.
- Oh, yeah.

18:06.729 --> 18:07.855
Thanks.

18:08.030 --> 18:09.827
Don't worry, I got your back.

18:10.466 --> 18:12.900
- Good night.
- Good night.

18:19.041 --> 18:21.168
What just happened?
